{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["The wonder is that a few of you will pursue a multitude of enemies. I have already informed you in Sefer Moznayim that ten and a hundred and a thousand and ten thousand—which is ten thousand—is a sum total, and the usage of increase is one-to-ten, as in 'for now they are as ten thousand to us,' and here He added that a hundred will pursue them, and five, and behold a doubling of the usage of increase, and each one of the hundred will pursue a hundred. Some say that because of the joining of the units the number increases, as in Lamentations: 'one will pursue a thousand.' And there is no need:" "<b>And your enemies shall fall.</b> A second time, that they fall time after time without recovery:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The Hebrew 'חמשה' after 'ירדפום' is textually difficult; it appears to mean that five from the hundred will do the pursuing, but the syntax is strained and may reflect corruption."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:39.546544801Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}